  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Inherit money, and the big fear is the taxman. But what's actually taken depends hugely on the size. Let's climb.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "home",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "home"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "$10K to $100M",
            "inherited."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "For almost everyone, the surprise is this. Below a huge threshold, the federal estate tax is zero.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "$13.6M",
          "label": "exemption — below it, $0 tax",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The federal estate tax only applies above a multi-million-dollar exemption.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-estatetax",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · estate tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So a normal inheritance of ten or a hundred thousand dollars is taxed federally at nothing.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "rows",
          "kicker": "Federal estate tax",
          "rows": [
            {
              "rank": "1",
              "name": "$10K–$1M",
              "value": "$0",
              "note": "well under the line",
              "color": "#1f7a3d",
              "bar": 0.2
            },
            {
              "rank": "2",
              "name": "$5M",
              "value": "$0",
              "note": "still exempt",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.4
            },
            {
              "rank": "3",
              "name": "$20M",
              "value": "~40%",
              "note": "on the excess",
              "color": "#17120f",
              "bar": 0.7
            },
            {
              "rank": "4",
              "name": "$100M",
              "value": "~40%",
              "note": "on most of it",
              "color": "#c0392b",
              "bar": 1.0
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A stepped-up basis can also wipe out decades of taxable gains.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-steppedup",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · stepped-up basis"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Only above the exemption does the roughly forty percent rate kick in, on the excess.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "~40%",
          "label": "only on the amount above",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "You can also gift eighteen thousand per person each year, tax-free.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-gifttax",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · gift tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Which is why the estate tax raises less than one percent of all federal revenue.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "<1% of revenue",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "For almost everyone, the real tax is spending it, not the government taking it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Spending is the tax",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Inheritance is simply assets passed on after death.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-inheritance",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · inheritance"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, are you surprised by how little most inheritances are actually taxed?",
